VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       glibc  does  not provide a wrapper for this system call.  You could in‐
       voke it using ssyyssccaallll(2).  But instead, you probably want  to  use  the
       iioo__ssuubbmmiitt() wrapper function provided by _l_i_b_a_i_o.

       Note  that  the  _l_i_b_a_i_o wrapper function uses a different type (_i_o___c_o_n_‐
       _t_e_x_t___t) for the _c_t_x___i_d argument.  Note also  that  the  _l_i_b_a_i_o  wrapper
       does  not follow the usual C library conventions for indicating errors:
       on error it returns a negated error number (the negative of one of  the
       values   listed  in  ERRORS).   If  the  system  call  is  invoked  via
       ssyyssccaallll(2), then the return value follows the usual conventions for in‐
       dicating an error: -1, with _e_r_r_n_o set to a (positive) value that  indi‐
       cates the error.

